{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcomes of each lottery, defined as the most favorable outcome with the lowest probability. For Lottery A, the outcomes are 4000 Euros (80%) and 0 Euros (20%). The most favorable outcome is 4000 Euros, which has a probability of 80%—this is the highest probability in this lottery, so it is not the least probable outcome. The least probable outcome in A is 0 Euros with 20%. For Lottery B, the outcome is 3000 Euros with 100% probability. Since there is only one outcome, it is both the most and least probable outcome by default, with 100% probability. The most favorable least probable outcome is therefore 3000 Euros (B) versus 0 Euros (A). According to the decision reason, Lottery B would be preferred because its least probable outcome (3000) is more favorable than that of A (0). Thus, the reason can be applied to the decision problem, and it would lead to choosing B.",
